 "first_response": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef solve(W=7000, L=13000, H=1500, u=4, b=10, q=4.5e-6):\n    # Compute volume and floor area of the box\n    V = W * L * H\n    A = W * L\n\n    # Calculate the residence time (V / Q), where Q = u * A (ventilation rate)\n    Q = u * A\n    tau = V / Q\n\n    # Compute SO2 concentration in the box using steady-state mass balance:\n    # Q*(b - c) = q*A\n    q_A = q * A\n    ratio = q_A / Q\n    c = b * (1 - ratio)\n\n    return {\n        \"1\": {\"value\": c * 1e6, \"unit\": \"\u03bcg/m\u00b3\"}  # single quantity in \u03bcg/m\u00b3\n    }\n```</s>"
